  "detail": "The issue asks to convert every `process.kill(pid, 0)` \"is gone\" assertion with the same race. These still assert that a killed or cancelled descendant makes kill(pid, 0) throw, so they can see a not-yet-reaped zombie: test/signal-confinement.test.ts:209 (owned descendant after timeout/cancel), test/hardening.test.ts:672 and :741 (cancelled writer), test/smoke.test.ts:1570 (completed attempt's child), and test/pipeline-delivery-privacy.test.ts:540 (cancelled scan child, `toThrow(... ESRCH)`). Convert them to expectProcessStopped. Leave assertions that a process is still alive (`expect(kill(control.pid, 0)).toBe(true)`) as they are."
 },
