  "id": "F2",
  "file": "test/process-support.ts",
  "line": 17,
  "title": "On Linux a missing stat file is accepted without confirming the process is gone",
  "detail": "expectProcessStopped returns on ENOENT/ESRCH from reading /proc/<pid>/stat. If procfs isn't mounted, or hides other users' processes (hidepid), a live process also gives ENOENT, so the helper passes for a running process, against the issue's requirement to stay strict about one. Before accepting a missing stat file, require `process.kill(pid, 0)` to fail with ESRCH (a zombie is already handled by the stat path); let any other outcome fail the assertion."
 }
]
